invariant: INV-55
file: handshake_post.c
catches: tcp_nonblocking_loop_test
reason: the KeyUpdate this side sends ends the peer's run, so a peer that
  asks for an answer and gets one each run sends KeyUpdates with no limit
  and no data. A tcp-blocking ch_read returns only data, so no write falls
  inside a run there, and bin/unit cannot see it. The tcp-nonblocking loop's
  server reads a full run of requests one a call, writes the answer, and
  requires CH_KEY_UPDATE_LIMIT for the next KeyUpdate.

--- old
    t->send_epochs++;
    t->key_update_owed = 0;
--- new
    t->send_epochs++;
    t->key_update_owed = 0;
    t->key_update_run = 0;
